  <h2>EU VAT context for German carts</h2>
  <p>
    Germany sits inside the EU customs union but still collects import VAT on many non-EU parcels.
    Read our general <a href="/blog/eu-import-vat-landed-cost-spreadsheet-buyers/">EU VAT landed cost</a> piece for parallel maths across member states.
    Pair with <a href="/blog/france-douane-kakobuy-spreadsheet-import-2026/">France customs guide</a> if you ship to multiple EU addresses.
  </p>

  <h2>Branded goods &amp; routing from China</h2>
  <p>
    German customs actively scrutinises trademark-heavy categories—bags, footwear, apparel logos.
    Spreadsheet rows do not include routing tags; you choose lines inside Kakobuy.
    Use <a href="/blog/shipping-branded-vs-unbranded-spreadsheet-restrictions/">branded vs. unbranded shipping</a> with realistic declared values before you promise friends a “steuerfrei” delivery.
  </p>

